      "content": "Light, then dust and a draft. You are alone in a damaged building: one wall cracked, rain staining the floor, the door half off its hinges. A blue panel hangs at eye level. Nobody came to greet you. No sword on a pedestal. Anything useful is salvage you choose to take. A draft finds the back of your neck. The panel is the only thing that treats you as real.\n\nYour blue panel waits on a designation. What name should it show?",
